       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling. The usual outpatient ceiling is 2,400 to 3,200 mg/day. A dose this high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, divided differently\n- Something else\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
